{"steps": [
  {"log": "DFM-HUD with TestMitter's fake Engo glasses (TestMX/devices/engo.lua) on its serial port: the config upload, select, then battery polls and gauge frames. TestMitter only: run with testmx-uid.lua --app DFM-HUD --script engo-test.jsn --model Abc --no-form --serial ttyUSB0=engo (GG_Abc.jsn has the gauges). HUD's form stays closed: it sends no gauges while a form is open"},
  {"expectState": "engo.connected", "value": true},

  {"log": "the glasses list only their system config, so HUD uploads config-fonts-images.txt and writes config DFM-HUD version 8 (Json/config-version.jsn)"},
  {"waitMessage": "Transfer complete", "anyTime": true, "timeout": "40s"},
  {"expectState": "engo.lastWrite", "value": "DFM-HUD v8"},
  {"expectState": "engo.configs.DFM-HUD", "value": 8},

  {"log": "then it selects its config and polls the battery once a second: the Status window shows the level and the green check"},
  {"waitText": "85%", "win": 2, "timeout": "20s"},
  {"expectState": "engo.current", "value": "DFM-HUD"},
  {"expectImage": "greencheck.png", "win": 2},
  {"expectNoImage": "redcross.png", "win": 2},

  {"log": "gauges flow for a while; every frame HUD wrote was well formed"},
  {"wait": "10s"},
  {"expectState": "engo.counts.x05", "min": 8},
  {"expectState": "engo.frames", "min": 300},
  {"expectState": "engo.bad", "value": 0},
  {"expectState": "engo.junk", "value": 0},
  {"log": "engo test finished"}
]}
